        "id": "12415064",
        "text": "In Japan, it is said that in the tenth month of the lunar calendar, all the gods of the country gather at Izumo-taisha, and so the tenth month, when the gods disappear from various regions, is called \"the month without gods\". However, in the Izumo region, where the gods gather, it is also called \"the month with gods\"."
